  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "What quantity must be added to the numbers 4, 18 and 60 to result in three numbers in geometric progression?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$3$",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the quantity added. Equal consecutive ratios give\n$$\\begin{align*}\n(18+x)^2 &= (4+x)(60+x)\\\\\nx^2+36x+324 &= x^2+64x+240\\\\\n324-240 &= 64x-36x\\\\\n84 &= 28x\\\\\nx &= 3.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe resulting numbers are $7,21,63$, with common ratio $3$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 55
  },
